  "notes": "{枯|か}れる is an intransitive verb ({自動詞|じどうし}). The transitive pair is {枯|か}らす (to let wither, to let dry up).\n\nASPECT ({ている}):\n{枯|か}れている indicates a resulting state of being withered or dried up.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {花|はな}/{草|くさ}が{枯|か}れる - flowers/grass withers\n- {木|き}が{枯|か}れる - a tree dies\n- {井戸|いど}/{川|かわ}が{枯|か}れる - well/river dries up\n- {声|こえ}が{枯|か}れる - voice becomes hoarse\n- {枯|か}れ{葉|は} - dead/fallen leaves\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {萎|しお}れる - to wilt (temporary, often recoverable)\n- {枯|か}れる is more permanent than {萎|しお}れる",
